From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Stay resumed until the USB controller
 powers on

Once the PHY's clocks no longer hold a runtime PM reference on the PHY
(the next change), the combo PHY runtime suspends, when userspace allows
it, whenever none of its PHYs holds a reference. dwc3 initialises the
PHY with phy_init(), soft-resets its core and only then calls
phy_power_on(). The PHY runtime suspends right after phy_init() has
dropped its reference, enters autonomous mode and turns off the clocks
the core reset needs: on a plug into an idle port "DWC3 controller soft
reset failed" is logged, the xHCI host is not created and the port stays
dead until the next boot.

qmp_combo_usb_init() already programs and starts the USB PHY, so the
USB PHY has had no power_on and power_off operations. Add them to record
whether the controller has powered the PHY on, and refuse runtime
suspend while USB or USB4 is initialised but not powered on. Autonomous
mode is then entered only for a PHY that its controller powered on and
released, as dwc3 does in its runtime suspend, and a PHY used for
DisplayPort alone is not held active.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index fabc92db09c..7b13f6a4295 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -2674,6 +2674,8 @@ struct qmp_combo {
 	struct phy *usb_phy;
 	enum phy_mode phy_mode;
 	unsigned int usb_init_count;
+	/* The USB controller has powered the USB PHY on. */
+	bool usb_powered_on;
 
 	struct phy *dp_phy;
 	unsigned int dp_aux_cfg;
@@ -4831,9 +4833,35 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb4_set_mode(struct phy *phy, enum phy_mode mode, int subm
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * qmp_combo_usb_init() already programs and starts the USB PHY. power_on and
+ * power_off only record whether the controller has taken it into use: dwc3
+ * resets its core between phy_init() and phy_power_on() and needs the PHY
+ * clocks until then.
+ */
+static int qmp_combo_usb_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct qmp_combo *qmp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(qmp->usb_powered_on, true);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int qmp_combo_usb_phy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct qmp_combo *qmp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(qmp->usb_powered_on, false);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct phy_ops qmp_combo_usb_phy_ops = {
 	.init		= qmp_combo_usb_init,
 	.exit		= qmp_combo_usb_exit,
+	.power_on	= qmp_combo_usb_phy_power_on,
+	.power_off	= qmp_combo_usb_phy_power_off,
 	.set_mode	= qmp_combo_usb_set_mode,
 	.owner		= THIS_MODULE,
 };
@@ -4928,6 +4956,16 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Autonomous mode is for a USB PHY that its controller has powered on
+	 * and then released. Between phy_init() and phy_power_on() the
+	 * controller still needs the PHY clocks: dwc3 resets its core there.
+	 * A PHY used for DisplayPort alone has no controller to wait for.
+	 */
+	if ((qmp->usb_init_count || qmp->usb4_init_count) &&
+	    !READ_ONCE(qmp->usb_powered_on))
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	qmp_combo_enable_autonomous_mode(qmp);
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(qmp->pipe_clk);
-- 
2.56.0

